WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.592 --> 00:00:05.928
· Perm: not needed if you already have thick hair.

2
00:00:06.264 --> 00:00:11.136
But if your hair is thin or fine and lacks body, consider getting a perm.

3
00:00:11.472 --> 00:00:15.000
About two weeks (15 days) before the ceremony is best.

4
00:00:15.336 --> 00:00:23.088
Too fresh a perm gets in the way of styling, and too old loses its hold, so two weeks out is the sweet spot when it settles in naturally.

5
00:00:23.424 --> 00:00:30.120
Go for a medium curl rather than a tight, frizzy one, and it helps to tell your stylist you're perming specifically for wedding-parent hair.

6
00:00:30.456 --> 00:00:34.536
· Color: about a week (7 days) before the ceremony is ideal.

7
00:00:34.872 --> 00:00:39.360
Too early and your roots may grow out enough to show gray again,

8
00:00:39.696 --> 00:00:45.624
while too close to the ceremony risks leftover dye marks on the scalp or an allergic reaction.

9
00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:51.936
Always perm first, then wait a week before coloring, to keep hair damage to a minimum.
